  "description": "Tree Maintenance Works - Cat 4 \rTree SW00628 - Liriodendron tulipifera in Middle Temple Garden\rSurvey comment - Adjacent building is scheduled for maintenance work requiring scaffolding which will impact the eastern canopy.\rRecommended to prune eastern canopy to give a 2m clearance from scaffolding\r- Using ladders and handsaw/ secateurs, sensitively reduce longer protruding elements of the eastern canopy from building by 2m,\rmaintaining natural flowing lines and shape and form. \r- All cuts to be made back to suitable secondary growth points \r\rTree SW00626 - Crataegus spp. in Middle Temple Garden\rSurvey comment - Adjacent building is scheduled for maintenance work requiring scaffolding which will impact the eastern canopy.\rRecommended to prune eastern canopy to give a 2m clearance from scaffolding\r- Using ladders and handsaw/ secateurs, sensitively reduce longer protruding elements of the eastern canopy from building by 2m,\rmaintaining natural flowing lines and shape and form. \r- All cuts to be made back to suitable secondary growth points \r\rTree SW00580 - London plane in Fountian Court \rSurvey comment - No Massaria evident at inspection. Tree is forming a low, structural limb at 4m south which is developing over the seating\rarea and if allowed to develop further will cause conflicts between tree and seating. Recommended to remove low branch and lift low canopy\rto provide 3m clearance\r- Remove low branch at 3m south and lift remaining canopy to 3m to an even level",
